Spring Boot REST API Notes
1. What is REST?

REST (Representational State Transfer) is an architectural style used to build web services that communicate over HTTP.

Features of REST
Stateless communication
Uses HTTP protocol
Supports multiple data formats (JSON, XML)
Lightweight and scalable
Platform independent
REST vs SOAP
REST	SOAP
Lightweight	Heavyweight
Uses HTTP	Uses HTTP, SMTP, TCP
JSON/XML	XML only
Faster	Slower
Easy to develop	Complex
2. HTTP Methods
Method	Purpose
GET	Retrieve data
POST	Create data
PUT	Update complete resource
PATCH	Partial update
DELETE	Remove resource
Example
GET /employees

Returns all employees.

GET /employees/101

Returns employee with ID 101.

POST /employees

Creates a new employee.

PUT /employees/101

Updates employee 101.

DELETE /employees/101

Deletes employee 101.

3. REST API Architecture
Client
   |
   v
Controller
   |
   v
Service
   |
   v
Repository
   |
   v
Database
4. Spring Boot REST API Dependencies
Maven Dependency
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
</dependency>
Optional JPA Dependency
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
</dependency>
5. Important REST Annotations
@RestController

Marks a class as REST Controller.

@RestController
public class EmployeeController {
}
@RequestMapping

Defines common URL mapping.

@RequestMapping("/employees")
@GetMapping

Handles GET requests.

@GetMapping
public List<Employee> getEmployees() {
    return service.getAllEmployees();
}
@PostMapping

Handles POST requests.

@PostMapping
public Employee addEmployee(@RequestBody Employee emp) {
    return service.save(emp);
}
@PutMapping

Handles PUT requests.

@PutMapping("/{id}")
public Employee updateEmployee(
        @PathVariable int id,
        @RequestBody Employee emp) {

    return service.update(id, emp);
}
@DeleteMapping

Handles DELETE requests.

@DeleteMapping("/{id}")
public String deleteEmployee(@PathVariable int id) {
    service.delete(id);
    return "Deleted Successfully";
}
6. RequestBody

Used to read JSON data from request body.

Request JSON
{
  "id":101,
  "name":"John",
  "salary":50000
}
Controller
@PostMapping
public Employee save(@RequestBody Employee emp) {
    return service.save(emp);
}
7. PathVariable

Used to extract values from URL.

@GetMapping("/{id}")
public Employee getEmployee(
        @PathVariable int id) {

    return service.findById(id);
}

Request:

GET /employees/101
8. RequestParam

Used to read query parameters.

@GetMapping("/search")
public Employee search(
        @RequestParam int id) {

    return service.findById(id);
}

Request:

GET /employees/search?id=101
9. ResponseEntity

Used to customize HTTP response.

@GetMapping("/{id}")
public ResponseEntity<Employee> getEmployee(
        @PathVariable int id) {

    Employee emp = service.findById(id);

    return ResponseEntity.ok(emp);
}
Different Responses
ResponseEntity.ok(data)

ResponseEntity.notFound().build()

ResponseEntity.status(201).body(data)

ResponseEntity.badRequest().build()
10. HTTP Status Codes
Code	Meaning
200	OK
201	Created
204	No Content
400	Bad Request
401	Unauthorized
403	Forbidden
404	Not Found
500	Internal Server Error
11. REST API Example
Entity
public class Employee {

    private int id;
    private String name;
    private double salary;

    // getters setters
}
Service
@Service
public class EmployeeService {

    private List<Employee> employees =
            new ArrayList<>();

    public List<Employee> getAllEmployees() {
        return employees;
    }

    public Employee save(Employee emp) {
        employees.add(emp);
        return emp;
    }
}
Controller
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/employees")
public class EmployeeController {

    @Autowired
    private EmployeeService service;

    @GetMapping
    public List<Employee> getEmployees() {
        return service.getAllEmployees();
    }

    @PostMapping
    public Employee addEmployee(
            @RequestBody Employee emp) {

        return service.save(emp);
    }
}
12. Exception Handling
Custom Exception
public class EmployeeNotFoundException
        extends RuntimeException {

    public EmployeeNotFoundException(
            String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
Global Exception Handler
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {

    @ExceptionHandler(
            EmployeeNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<String> handleException(
            EmployeeNotFoundException ex) {

        return ResponseEntity
                .status(HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND)
                .body(ex.getMessage());
    }
}
13. Validation
Dependency
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
    <artifactId>
        spring-boot-starter-validation
    </artifactId>
</dependency>
Entity Validation
public class Employee {

    @NotNull
    private Integer id;

    @NotBlank
    private String name;

    @Min(1000)
    private double salary;
}
Controller
@PostMapping
public Employee save(
        @Valid @RequestBody Employee emp) {

    return service.save(emp);
}
14. Consuming REST APIs using RestTemplate
@Autowired
private RestTemplate restTemplate;

Employee emp =
    restTemplate.getForObject(
        "http://localhost:8080/employees/1",
        Employee.class);
15. Consuming REST APIs using WebClient
WebClient webClient =
        WebClient.create();

Employee emp =
    webClient.get()
             .uri("/employees/1")
             .retrieve()
             .bodyToMono(Employee.class)
             .block();
16. Testing REST APIs
Using Postman
Create Request
Select HTTP Method
Enter URL
Add JSON Body
Send Request
Verify Response

Example:

{
  "id":101,
  "name":"John",
  "salary":50000
}
