REST API Best Practices
Use nouns in URLs (/employees, /orders)
Use proper HTTP methods
Return meaningful HTTP status codes
Validate input data
Handle exceptions globally
Version APIs (/api/v1/employees)
Keep APIs stateless
Use DTOs instead of exposing entities directly
Document APIs using Swagger/OpenAPI

These notes cover the complete Spring Boot REST API flow typically taught in Java Full Stack training and are suitable for interviews as well as hands-on development